# Harness screenshots. sys30.py writes every fixture's final frame to
# ./sys30-shots by default (-o), and run.py's --keep does the same; they are
# evidence for one run, not repository content. 69 of them were committed
# once, inside a commit about something else.
sys30-shots/
shots/

# Build outputs
build/
*.o
*.a
macextract

# Fixture archives are copyrighted software — never committed.
# Only manifests + SOURCES.md (provenance) are tracked.
fixtures/*
!fixtures/manifests/
!fixtures/SOURCES.md

# Reference material is fetched by tools/fetch_references.sh, not committed.
reference/
build-mac/
build-mac-*/

# Python bytecode. Anchored at the repo root rather than at tools/, because
# tools/vmac/ and tools/quickdraw-repro/ each import the other's modules and so
# generate their own __pycache__ — three of which got committed before this.
**/__pycache__/

# The bootstrap distribution IS committed, from 2026-08-07: it is the download
# for people who have an old Mac and no way to compile anything, and this
# repository has no other release channel. Rebuild it with tools/make_dist.sh
# and commit the result whenever the application changes — a stale binary here
# is worse than none, and has happened before (see the comment at the top of
# make_dist.sh).
